<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5109" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμείλ-ικτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μειλίσσω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unsoftened, harsh, cruel,</i> of words, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.137
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.98
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.
				</span></i>
			 Tyr.<i><span class="en">
				12.6
			</span></i>; of fetters, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				659
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίτοι,</span> of the thread of
			Clotho, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(7).301
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					13p.448M.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons, =
			sq., <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.337
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				4.26
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, ἔχειν τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.298
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Syrian.
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				42.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοίρας ἀτυχούσης
			ἀμειλίκτως,</span> of <i>pitiless</i> fate, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				4.54
			</span></i>.</div>
